WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.399
I want to talk today about the issue of transgender
sports participation and maybe even more specifically

00:00:06.399 --> 00:00:11.860
about trans women in sports, and there's a
really specific reason why I want to do this.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.100
Last week, I got a call, and as many of you
know, when we do calls, they can be about

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.100
anything.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.100
I'm not prepared for them.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.100
I'm just answering.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.100
And the topics can be anything.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.120
And I give my thoughts at the time.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:27.190
And someone called in who said they're on
the left, they're not trans phobic.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:30.119
They support trans rights at every opportunity.

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:36.700
And yet they said they recognize that having
individuals born biologically male participating

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.050
in women's sports confers an advantage at
a physical level that didn't make sense to

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.050
them.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:48.239
And I said not knowing a lot about it, that
I also didn't fully understand the logic.

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:53.440
But I was aware of the fact that the right
often cynically wants to make this the issue

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.979
about trans rights when the reality is it's
really not the major issue that that that

00:00:57.979 --> 00:00:59.550
make it out to be.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:04.409
And it's often used as a way to subtly push
back against trans rights more broadly.

00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:08.490
And today, I want to expand on my comments
because I actually had some time over the

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.020
weekend to research the issue in more detail.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:16.590
And the more I learn about it, the more convinced
I am that it is a fabricated wedge issue to

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:21.820
divide people and in particular to predispose
people to be against trans rights.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:27.540
As I researched the issue, one of the things
I learned is that hormone replacement therapy,

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:32.890
which trans women often avail themselves of
over a one to two year period, comes close

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:39.260
to completely eliminating the performance
gap that we might imagine exists in some sports.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:44.079
When you have individuals born biologically
male competing against those born biologically

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:45.079
female.

00:01:45.079 --> 00:01:49.780
Now, I want to put aside for a second the
absolutely hysterical notion that some CIS

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:56.330
gendered men might, quote, pretend to be trans
women and go through testosterone blocking

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:02.979
treatment merely to compete in women's sports
without actually genuinely being trans.

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:07.119
Someone willing to do that has bigger issues
that need to be resolved.

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:11.750
But it's it's so uncommon that it's not really
the issue.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:18.470
The reality is that a study from 2015 called
Race Times for Transgender Athletes shows

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:23.440
that trans women have essentially no advantage
in running over CIS gendered women after a

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.120
period of roughly a year of hormone replacement
therapy.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:32.400
There's another more recent study which showed
that after one year, there is still a modest

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.690
advantage for trans women and that the length
of time with the hormone replacement therapy

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.280
maybe should be longer.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:45.010
But to get from that, the idea that this is
some kind of, you know, woak kabal looking

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:51.830
to impose Mike Tyson or his physical equivalent
into women's wrestling against 18 year old

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:58.550
girls as an example, that's a cartoon that
that's ridiculous to suggest that that's predominantly

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.810
the situation that that exists in the world.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:06.380
And I got a few dozen emails about this, and
I was completely genuine when I said last

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:13.070
week, I've not studied this enough, but at
face value, it does raise some questions for

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:14.070
me.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:19.710
I still believe this is a complicated issue,
but the issue of trans sports is one of many

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:23.990
issues related to trans rights, and its importance
is being dramatically inflated by certain

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:26.800
groups of people for cynical political goals.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:33.010
And what I mean by that is that trans people,
intersex individuals, they didn't just start

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:38.780
existing in the last five years, sports organizations,
endocrinologists and others, they've known

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.090
about this for a really long time.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:44.700
And many institutions deal with these things
on a case by case basis.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:50.280
So when I hear about a political movement
that has this knee jerk reaction to immediately

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:56.420
say no trans women and women's sports, period,
it either is coming from just an ignorant

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.170
place or a place of very bad faith.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:02.720
So I'm glad to have learned more about it
and to be able to say more.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.650
And that doesn't mean all my questions are
answered with a whole bunch of sports.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:11.200
This is not really an issue with a certain
category of sports.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.970
This is in theory an issue.

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:17.480
And we have to look at hormone replacement
therapy, actual performance differences after

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.410
one or two year periods.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:24.310
And I tweeted about this yesterday and a few
people wrote to me and they said, oh, but

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:29.230
there's this particular case where someone's
skull was broken by a trans woman.

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:32.840
OK, I'm not saying that there are no issues.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:40.690
What I am saying is that pretending this is
the issue about trans rights is wrong.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:44.440
I'm not going to say necessarily that it's
coming from bad faith.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:48.070
It could be ignorance, but it's wrong to say
this is the issue.

00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:50.530
It has to be dealt with on a case by case
basis.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:54.720
And the other thing I would point out is the
people that were replying to my.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:05:01.880
We kept talking about the two or three individual
instances, where else would these folks say

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:06.930
that because of two or three instances of
something, we need to completely change all

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:11.910
of the legal and regulatory infrastructure,
look at the number of people that are killed

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:12.910
by guns.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.470
And yet they say, oh, yeah, but I mean, you
know, a few hundred incidents, that's that's

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:19.380
not enough to justify changing the rules.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:22.990
But yet here everybody's pointing to the same
two or three incidents over the last five

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:28.389
years and saying that justifies creating an
entirely new regulatory and legal apparatus.

00:05:28.389 --> 00:05:30.240
It just doesn't pass the sniff test for me.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:34.720
And I've been glad to to learn more about
it doesn't mean every question is answered,

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:39.400
doesn't mean that there aren't some problems
to solve or questions to deal with.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:43.500
But I think we need to understand the sort
of cynical nature that exists by among those

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:51.480
who pretend this is the issue and use it as
a smokescreen to deny trans rights more broadly.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:52.630
And unfortunately, that's what's happening
all too often.

